# Project Overview

## Project Summary
This project is a university administration and student portal for University of New York Tirana. It combines a public-facing website, an admin dashboard, and student-facing tools in one system.

The platform is built around live records for students, professors, courses, enrollments, payments, finance, feedback, news, questions, notifications, and users.

## Goals / Objectives
- Reduce manual admin work by automating student, enrollment, and finance workflows.
- Give staff one central place to manage students, professors, courses, payments, feedback, and announcements.
- Help students access enrollment, academic, and support information faster.
- Keep financial tracking clear with income, expenses, balances, and payment history.
- Present the university with a modern, consistent digital brand.

## What Success Looks Like
- Admins can find and update records quickly without switching between tools.
- Students can view key information and complete common tasks with fewer steps.
- Finance data stays accurate across enrollments, payments, income, and expenses.
- Feedback and news are visible in the dashboard instead of being scattered.
- The interface feels clean, premium, and easy to use on desktop and mobile.

## KPIs / Targets
Current seeded baseline from the system:
- 2 students
- 2 professors
- 2 courses
- 1 active enrollment
- 2 payment transactions
- 1 income record
- 1 expense record
- 1 feedback record
- 1 news item
- 2 notifications
- 6 demo user accounts across 6 roles

Recommended operational targets:
- Reduce admin work by 40% through better record management and automation.
- Increase student engagement by making dashboard access and support information faster to reach.
- Improve response time for searching records and viewing summaries.
- Keep finance and enrollment records in sync with zero manual balance mismatch.

## Target Users
- Admin
- Supervisor
- Advisor
- Professor
- Student
- Normal user / guest

## Key Features
The most valuable features in the system are:
- Student management with balances, profiles, and status tracking.
- Enrollment management with course linkage, coupon handling, and payment verification.
- Payments and ledger tracking for credits and debits.
- Finance tracking for income, expenses, total income, total expenses, and net income.
- Dashboard overview with recent students, recent feedback, recent income, and recent expenses.
- Courses and professor management.
- News and notifications for university updates.
- Questions and feedback tools for student support.
- Role-based access so users only see the tools they should use.

## Benefits / Value
Why people should care:
- Saves time for admin staff.
- Better user experience for students and staff.
- More efficient management of university records.
- Clearer financial control and reporting.
- Less paperwork and fewer manual processes.
- A more modern university brand image.
- Faster access to information for daily operations.

## Real System Data Snapshot
The current system is already structured around these live modules and data tables:
- Students
- Professors
- Users
- Courses
- Enrollments
- Payments
- Income
- Expenses
- Feedback
- News
